      "independent_solution": "a) Write numerator n and denominator d with all denominators nonzero. (n+2)/(d+3)=n/d implies 3n=2d, so the original value is 2/3. The second relation gives (n+1)/(d+6)=1/2; substituting n=2d/3 yields d=12,n=8, original fraction 8/12. b) d=2n-1 from (n+1)/(d+3)=1/2. The product condition is 5n(n-1)=d(d+1)=2n(2n-1), hence n(n-3)=0. n=0,d=-1 makes d+1=0 and is inadmissible; n=3,d=5 gives 3/5.",
