      "independent_solution": "a) Let first speed u, second speed v, first premeeting hours t; second premeeting t-1. Second premeeting distance is 2.5u, first is 2.5u+2, so t=2.5+2/u. After meeting first takes 2.5 h and second takes 2.4 h (arrival 0.1 h earlier), hence 2.4v=2.5u+2. Also v(t-1)=2.5u. Elimination gives 9u^2-32u-16=0, u=4 or -4/9. Positive solution u=4,v=5 km/h, total distance 5u+2=22 km. b) Bus premeeting time t, motorcycle t-0.5. Motorcycle postmeeting 1 h, bus 1.5 h. ut=v, v(t-0.5)=1.5u; t(t-0.5)=1.5 gives t=1.5 (negative root rejected). v=1.5u,90=u(1.5+1.5), so bus 30, motorcycle 45 km/h.",
